{
    "$schema": "vendor/infection/infection/resources/schema.json",
    "source": {
        "directories": ["src"]
    },
    "logs": {
        "text": "php://stderr",
        "summary": "build/infection-summary.log"
    },
    "testFramework": "testo",
    // ER-003 attribution sweep. src/Exception/InvalidArgumentException.php was
    // named in zero test's #[Covers(...)], so it was silently excluded from
    // mutation attribution regardless of the tests that already throw/catch it
    // (ValidationTest, LabelSetTest, InMemoryMeterTest, NullMeterTest). Fixed by
    // adding #[Covers(InvalidArgumentException::class)] to those four test
    // classes — attribution-only, not a mutant-count fix: confirmed empirically
    // (`infection --filter=InvalidArgumentException.php`, both before and after
    // the #[Covers] change) that 0 mutations are generated either way. The class
    // body is `final class InvalidArgumentException extends \InvalidArgumentException {}`,
    // a bare marker with no statements to mutate.
    //
    // While in here, also closed 11 pre-existing escapes surfaced by the same
    // full run (Escaped 16 -> 5, Total 150 -> 150, Covered MSI 89% -> 96%) with
    // targeted assertions: InMemoryMeter name-validation on all four factories,
    // gauge/histogram memoization identity, InMemoryGauge's fresh-key baseline
    // (`?? 0.0`), NullMeter gauge/histogram name-validation, NullUpDownCounter
    // singleton identity, and MetricSnapshot::equals() detecting a mismatch past
    // the first sorted sample. The remaining 5 are genuine equivalents, named
    // individually — not tests, not ignores:
    //   - InMemoryHistogram.php:37 ArrayItemRemoval (`'count' => 0.0,` dropped
    //     from the initial array literal). `$this->data[$key]['count'] += 1.0`
    //     always runs on every observe() regardless, so a missing key
    //     auto-vivifies from null to the same 1.0 as an explicit 0.0 baseline
    //     would — PHP's `null + 1.0 === 0.0 + 1.0`. No observable output differs.
    //   - InMemoryHistogram.php:40 DecrementInteger (`array_fill(0, n, 0.0)` ->
    //     `array_fill(-1, n, 0.0)`). This only relabels the internal bucket
    //     array's keys (shifts one extra, unused `-1` key in; drops the last
    //     real index, `n-1`, which maps to the `+Inf` bound). `snapshot()`
    //     re-reads buckets strictly through `$this->bounds`' own 0..n-1 index
    //     sequence, so the stray `-1` key is never read. The dropped `n-1` key
    //     (`+Inf`) always auto-vivifies to the correct count because every
    //     observation satisfies `value <= INF`, i.e. that bucket is touched on
    //     every single call — same reasoning as the mutant above. No bucket
    //     value a test can observe ever differs.
    //   - LabelSet.php:36 MatchArmRemoval (`\is_string($value) => $value,` arm
    //     dropped from the label-value match, falling through to
    //     `default => (string) $value`). For a string input, `(string) $value`
    //     is the identity cast — same output either way.
    //   - MetricSnapshot.php:55 Spaceship (`$a <=> $b` reversed to `$b <=> $a`
    //     in the private `sortedSamples()` comparator). It is used only inside
    //     `equals()`, symmetrically, on both operands' own sample lists. Any
    //     consistent total order — ascending or descending — puts the same-key
    //     samples from `$this` and `$other` at matching indices, so the
    //     positional comparison in `equals()` is unaffected by the direction.
    //   - RedMetricsMiddleware.php:73 CastString (`(string) $response->getStatusCode()`
    //     -> the cast dropped, `$status` stays `int`). `$status` is only ever
    //     consumed as `LabelSet`'s `'status'` value, and `LabelSet`'s
    //     constructor already stringifies any non-bool/non-string scalar via its
    //     own `default => (string) $value` match arm — the explicit cast here is
    //     redundant with that downstream coercion, not a behavioral difference.
    "minMsi": 85,
    "mutators": {
        "@default": true
    }
}
